  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating and comparing the skewness of the two lotteries, which involves assessing how probability mass is distributed between favorable and unfavorable outcomes. The individual, however, does not reference probabilities or distributional shape at all. Instead, the justification is based on a philosophical or motivational attitude toward winning and losing, not on structural features of the lotteries. There is no evidence that the individual considered which lottery has more probability on unfavorable outcomes, nor that they preferred one based on being more right-skewed. The reasoning in the report is fundamentally different in kind from the skewness-based reason. Therefore, it is unlikely that the individual used the skewness reason.",
